# SlayZone Env Vars — Target State (post-simplification)

The env vars that actually exist (read from `process.env`) once the simplification lands. Deleted/derived-away vars are NOT listed — they no longer exist as env vars. Precedence: `env var > ~/.slayzone config.json > generated/default`.

Two flags produce the three value columns: **`SLAYZONE_SUPERVISED`** (host-set → Supervised) and **`SLAYZONE_MODE=local|remote`** (operator-set → Standalone vs Remote). `remote` sets the whole hardening bundle (hub: auth+TLS; runner: wss+cert-pin); `local` (default) = loopback, auth off. Supervised is always `local` exposure.

## Single anchor: `SLAYZONE_ROOT`

One optional var anchors all on-disk state for hub AND runner. Default = CWD (standalone) / `$HOME/.slayzone` (supervised). Relocate = `cd /srv/slayzone && slayzone-hub` or `SLAYZONE_ROOT=/srv/slayzone`.

```
SLAYZONE_ROOT
├── slayzone.sqlite     (hub DB)
├── config.json         (carries: allowedRoots + the env-mirrored keys below)
├── logs/
└── runner/             (runner post-enroll creds)
```

Hub and runner are separate servers with separate CWDs → separate `SLAYZONE_ROOT`s. Non-env-var config that lives ONLY in `<ROOT>/config.json`: `allowedRoots` (runner FS jail — default `[ROOT]` + operator-listed project dirs; locally-declared, never hub-pushed).

